        <body>
            <div xml:id="d448">

                <pb facs="0540" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg460"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1987.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the embassy’s dispatch No.
                    1814 of December 31, 1901, I have the honor to append hereto a memorandum report
                    of certain military cases, more particularly mentioned below, which have not
                    been the subject of previous correspondence or which have been settled during
                    the quarter ending to-day. There were no military cases to report for the
                    quarter ending March 30 last.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">And. D. White.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d448-a1.xml" xpointer="d448-a1"/>
